Package: disparpdf
Architecture: any
Provides: diffpdf (= ${binary:Version})
Breaks: diffpdf (<< 1:1.1.1-1~)
Replaces: diffpdf (<< 1:1.1.1-1~)
Description: compare two PDF files textually or visually
 disparPDF compares two PDF files, page by page, and shows their
 differences side by side.  By default the comparison is of the words on
 each pair of pages, but comparing character by character (e.g., for
 logographic languages) and comparing the appearance of the pages (for
 example, if a diagram is changed or a paragraph reformatted) are also
 supported.  Particular pages or page ranges can be compared, and each
 page of one file can be paired with a page further on in the other, for
 when pages have been inserted or removed.  The differences can be saved
 as a PDF file.
 .
 Batch mode (disparPDF --batch, or disparPDFc) compares without a window
 or display, printing a result code, and can save the differences as PDF
 and a report as XML.  Pages are compared in parallel.
 .
 disparPDF is a fork of ConfrontaPDF, itself a fork of DiffPDF.

Package: diffpdf
Architecture: all
Section: oldlibs
Depends: disparpdf (>= ${source:Version})
Description: compare two PDF files textually or visually -- transitional package
 DiffPDF is no longer maintained; this package now installs disparPDF,
 a fork of it, which also provides the diffpdf command.  This package
 can safely be removed.
